        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2023",
        "question_text": "<p>To bisect a given line AB, which of the following steps is <b>not</b> required?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Bisecting a line AB requires using a compass to draw arcs from points A and B with the same radius, intersecting above and below the line. The correct bisector is drawn through these intersections. <b>Drawing a perpendicular line from point A alone is not part of the standard bisection process.</b></p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "44515",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Draw arcs from A and B with the same radius",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "20538",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "Draw a perpendicular line from point A only",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "45601",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "Join the intersection points of the arcs",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "32909",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "Use a compass to mark equal distances from A and B",
